# fm84 magyarul.
#
# Each msgid is the English as the code has it, and the msgstr under it what
# is shown in its place. A sentence with a count in it has a msgstr for each
# form the count takes: [one] for 1, [other] for the rest - a noun after a
# number stays singular, so the two are mostly alike. A msgctxt sets one use
# of a word apart from the same word elsewhere. {name} is a place the
# program fills, kept as it is, and never given a case ending: the
# sentences are made so that it needs none. The letters to press - Y, N, A
# and the like - stay as they are. Names are quoted „thus”.

